==Trivia==
*Goblins are small, grotesque, monstrous creatures that appear in the folklore of multiple European cultures. First attested in stories from the Middle Ages, they are ascribed conflicting abilities, temperaments, and appearances depending on the story and country of origin, ranging from mischievous household spirits to malicious, bestial thieves. They often have magical abilities similar to a fairy or demon, such as the ability to shapeshift. Similar creatures include [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duende duendes], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kobold kobolds], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leprechaun leprechauns], and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghoul ghouls].
**In the German and Dutch language setting of the game, the Goblin Giant's name translates to "Kobold Giant". In the Spanish, Arabic, and Vietnamese language setting of the game, the Goblin Giant's name translates to "Duende Giant", "Giant Ghoul", and "Giant Leprechaun" respectively.
**The Goblin Giant is 1 of 17 [[cards]] associated with [[Goblins]], with the others being [[Spear Goblins]], [[Goblin Gang]], [[Baby Goblins]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Goblin Demolisher]], [[Suspicious Bush]], [[Goblin Cage]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Goblin Barrel]], [[Goblin Curse]], [[Goblin Drill]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Party Rocket]], [[Party Hut]], [[Goblinstein]], and of course, Goblins.
*The Goblin Giant is one of the first [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] cards to receive a card render, alongside the [[Archers]], [[Knight]], Goblins, [[Bomber]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Flying Machine]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Royal Hogs]], Dart Goblin, [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], [[Balloon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Goblin Giant is one of the first cards to be featured in the [[Season Shop]], alongside the Goblins and Goblin Cage.
*The Goblin Giant is 1 of 14 troops that has been featured with a [[Buff#Rage|Rage]] [[buff]], the others being [[Electro Spirit]], Giant, Zappies, [[Guards]], Giant Skeleton, Electro Dragon, Wall Breakers, [[Electro Giant]], Mega Knight, Ram Rider, [[Electro Wizard]], [[Sparky]], and Royal Ghost.
*The Goblin Giant is 1 of 15 troops which bring an excited reaction from the audience upon spawning and brings a collective groan from the audience when defeated, as well as a concerning gasp when the opponent plays him, the others include [[Royal Giant]], Giant, P.E.K.K.A., Giant Skeleton, [[Rune Giant]], [[Golem]], Bowler, Electro Wizard, [[Inferno Dragon]], Sparky, Lava Hound, Night Witch, [[Super Lava Hound]], and the [[Monk]].
*The Goblin Giant is 1 of 2 troops with the “Ranged Ground & Air targeting unit riding on Melee Building targeting unit” pattern, the other being Ram Rider.
*The Goblin Giant is 1 of 10 cards to have an alliterative name, the others being the Royal Recruits, Goblin Gang, [[Mega Minion]], Cannon Cart, [[Barbarian Barrel]], Ram Rider, [[Dagger Duchess]], [[Boss Bandit]], and the [[Mighty Miner]].
* While not available as a troop in Clash of Clans, the Goblin Giant may have inspired the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Yeti Yeti], a troop from the former as they share similarities.
*The Goblin Giant's hat is very similar to the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Builder Builder]'s from Clash of Clans.
*His [[Star Points|Star Level 3 Skin]] grants the Spear Goblins a red mohawk similar to the Level 6 Goblin in Clash of Clans.
*There is a [[Loading Screen Hints|Loading Screen Hint]] that says: "''Somebody once told Goblin Giant that the world was gonna roll him.''" This is a reference to the alternative rock song "[https://youtu.be/5xxQs34UMx4 All Star]", by the Smash Mouth, which was used in the beginning of the Shrek movie. This is a reference to the fact that Goblin Giant resembles Shrek.
*The Goblin Giant is the subject of 2 [[Emotes]].

